# FORGE Agent Guide

PostgreSQL-only infrastructure. **Package: `forgex`** (not `forge`). [Full docs](https://tryforge.dev/docs) | `forge --help` | `forge.toml` for config.

## Run

```bash
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env; [ -f frontend/.env ] || cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
docker compose up --build  # Starts backend, frontend, postgres
```

## Function Selection

| Need | Use | Note |
|------|-----|------|
| Read data | Query | Cacheable, subscribable, no side effects |
| Write data | Mutation | Transactional, atomic, triggers reactivity |
| External API | Action | Non-transactional, has `ctx.http()` |
| Async work | Job | Retryable, progress tracking |
| Scheduled | Cron | Time-based, catch-up support, leader-only |
| Multi-step | Workflow | Durable, suspendable, compensatable |

## Backend Patterns

```rust
// All contexts
ctx.db()                          ctx.require_user_id()?
ctx.dispatch_job(name, args)      ctx.start_workflow(name, input)

// Attributes (see docs for full options)
#[forgex::query]                  // + cache="30s", public, rate_limit(...)
#[forgex::mutation]               // + timeout=30, require_role("admin")
#[forgex::action]                 // + timeout=60
#[forgex::job]                    // + #[retry(...)], #[priority], #[idempotent]
#[forgex::cron("0 * * * *")]      // + #[timezone], #[catch_up]
#[forgex::workflow]               // + #[version], #[timeout]

// Job: ctx.progress(50, "msg")?; ctx.heartbeat().await?;
// Cron: ctx.log.info("msg", json!({...}));
// Workflow: ctx.step("name", || async {...}).run().await?;
//           ctx.sleep(Duration).await?; ctx.parallel().step(...).run().await?;
```

## Anti-Patterns

| Don't | Do |
|-------|-----|
| External API in Mutation | Use Action |
| `tokio::sleep` in Workflow | `ctx.sleep()` (durable) |
| Destructure `$props()` | Keep reference |
| Poll with `query()` loop | `subscribe()` |
| Skip `ctx.heartbeat()` | Call in long loops |
| `ctx.auth.user_id().unwrap()` | `ctx.require_user_id()?` |

## Schema

```rust
#[forgex::model]
pub struct Task { pub id: Uuid, pub status: TaskStatus, pub created_at: DateTime<Utc> }

#[forgex::forge_enum]
pub enum TaskStatus { Pending, InProgress, Completed }
```
Generates TypeScript types. DB uses sqlx. Schema (indexes, constraints) → migrations.

## Structure

```
src/main.rs              # ForgeBuilder, registrations
src/schema/              # #[forgex::model]
src/functions/           # One file per function (queries, mutations, jobs, crons, workflows)
frontend/src/lib/forge/  # Generated (forge generate)
```

## Workflow: Schema → Migration (`migrations/NNNN_name.sql` with `-- @up`/`-- @down`) → Function (`forge add <type> <name>`) → Register in main.rs → `forge generate`

## Auth

```rust
#[forgex::query(public)]                    // No auth
#[forgex::mutation(require_role("admin"))]  // Role required
ctx.require_user_id()?                      // Uuid or error
ctx.auth.user_id()                          // Option<Uuid>
ctx.auth.has_role("x")                      // bool
ctx.auth.claim("key")                       // Custom JWT claim
```

## Frontend (Svelte 5)

```svelte
let props = $props();  // NEVER destructure at module level
const users = subscribe(getUsers, {});     // Real-time
const data = await query(getUsers, {});    // One-time
await mutate(createUser, { name, email }); // Write
const job = createJobTracker<Args>('type', apiUrl); job.start({...});
```

## Testing

```bash
cargo test --features embedded-db  # Uses embedded PostgreSQL (recommended)
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://... cargo test  # Uses external database
```

```rust
// Import testing utilities directly from forge_core
use forge_core::testing::{TestQueryContext, TestMutationContext, TestDatabase};
use forge_core::{assert_ok, assert_err, assert_job_dispatched};

let ctx = TestQueryContext::authenticated(user_id);
let ctx = TestQueryContext::builder().as_user(id).with_role("admin").build();
let ctx = TestActionContext::builder().mock_http_json("url/*", json!({...})).build();
let db = TestDatabase::embedded().await?;  // Requires embedded-db feature
assert_job_dispatched!(ctx, "name"); assert_workflow_started!(ctx, "name");
```

## Code Quality

Idiomatic Rust | Testability (inject via context) | Fail fast (`require_*`) | Small functions (<30 lines) | No premature abstraction | Design out edge cases | Structured logging | Comments explain why

**Always use CLI:** `forge add <type> <name>` to generate functions. **Always run after changes:** Run `cargo clippy -- -D warnings && cargo test --features embedded-db && bun lint && bun format` to verify.

## Advanced (see docs)

- **Rate Limiting:** `#[forgex::query(rate_limit(requests=100, per="1m", key="user"))]`
- **Multi-Tenancy:** `ctx.tenant_id()`, `ctx.require_tenant()`
- **Clustering:** `forge.toml` → `[node]` roles, worker_capabilities
